<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat- Prices steady, trade slow.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat- Prices steady, trade slow.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spring wheat prices were little changed Tuesday in quiet conditions with bullish sentiment among farmers keeping movement slow.</p>
<p>&quot;The farmers are still bullish and are holding on to their wheat,&quot; one Montana dealer said.</p>
<p>Basis levels were also steady with the key MGE May spring wheat futures ending up 1/4 cent at $4.00-1/2 a bushel.</p>
<p>Export news was scarce although USDA's CCC announced a tender for 9,600 tonnes of white wheat for Yemen and up to 10,950 tonnes number two or better hard red winter or hard red spring wheat for Jordan.  </p>
